From b4bc2e5d2d6694b8c3cd1ea832dc5e6e19a34f50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 21:09:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 112/114] core: make the public headers self-contained

28 public headers take a 'struct ofono_modem *' without the tag having
been declared. In-tree that is harmless, because ofono.h pulls in modem.h
first. Out of tree it is not: a plugin that includes, say, radio-settings.h
before modem.h gets a struct declared inside a parameter list, which C
scopes to that prototype alone. The result is 'expected struct ofono_modem *
but argument is of type struct ofono_modem *', which is as confusing as it
sounds.

Add the forward declaration to each of them.

(cherry picked from commit bec68820a2672cddd3587666d5a583dba865bf93)
Upstream-Status: Pending
